# Experient Backend — .env.example
#
# Shared secrets (AGENTS_INTERNAL_KEY, AI keys, DATABASE_URL, etc.) live in the
# ROOT .env.example one level up. This file is for backend-only overrides.
# In local dev, a single root .env is sufficient — you do not need this file.
#
# If you need to override a root .env value for the backend only, copy this file
# to backend/.env and set the value here (backend .env is loaded AFTER root .env,
# so values here take precedence for the backend process).

# ── Backend-only overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=3001
# BACKEND=local
# SKIP_AUTH=true    # LOCAL DEV ONLY

# ── All other vars live in root .env ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# See /.env.example for DATABASE_URL, AGENTS_INTERNAL_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, etc.
# Workflow Automation vars (WORKFLOW_CREDENTIALS_KEY, ZENDESK_*, WORKFLOW_TRIGGER_STREAM,
# WORKFLOW_RETRY_*, WORKFLOW_MAX_ATTEMPTS) live in the root file's "Workflow Automation
# (Xperiq Actions)" section.
#
# WORKFLOW_CONNECTOR_TIMEOUT_MS and WORKFLOW_EXECUTING_TIMEOUT_MIN (added 2026-07-01,
# Kenji's chaos-pass fixes) could not be added to the root file in THIS session — the
# sandbox denied that write here even though a prior session's write to the same file
# succeeded (see docs/automation-hub/ADR_EXECUTION_ARCHITECTURE.md's review addendum).
# Documented here as the fallback per docs/ENV_VARS.md convention; someone with root
# write access should move these two lines into the root file's existing Workflow
# Automation section (after WORKFLOW_MAX_ATTEMPTS) and delete this override block.
# WORKFLOW_CONNECTOR_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# WORKFLOW_EXECUTING_TIMEOUT_MIN=5
